  "gaps": [
    "TEC 100 Computer Literacy is named as the BSIT replacement for GEN 102, but its credit value is not printed; 3 credits is assumed only because it replaces the 3-credit GEN 102.",
    "The program states 3 credits from the major (ECO 203, marked *) may also satisfy Global Campus Foundations requirements (33 + 57 + 33 = 123 vs. 120 total), but the capture does not say which specific Foundations course ECO 203 replaces.",
    "The Global Campus Foundations sequence is described as the 'standard' and 'Courses may be substituted'; allowed substitutions are not listed in the capture.",
    "GEN 101 (3 credits) is scheduled first and counts toward electives; students with fewer than 30 transferable credits also take GEN 104 (3 credits, elective). How these are applied within the 33 elective credits is not itemized for this program.",
    "INT 499 lists INT 302 as a prerequisite, but INT 302 does not appear in the BSIT course list in the capture.",
    "INT 499 is marked '^ This course must be taken last in the program'; the capture does not state that it must be completed at UAGC.",
    "Residency: a minimum of 30 credits must be completed at the University as a matriculated student; which courses count toward residency is not specified.",
    "Upper-division requirement: minimum 30 upper-division credits, including 18 in the major; the capture does not define which course numbers count as upper-division.",
    "Minimum cumulative GPA of 2.00 is required for graduation; no BSIT-specific grade minimums per course are printed."
  ],
